{
    "word": "wetmatigheid",
    "lang_code": "nl",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [],
        "ru-extract.jsonl": [],
        "nl-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "1ee75e82-1f64-3355-8862-518387408f7f",
                "word": "wetmatigheid",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "nl",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "8f56d78b-9b96-4eb5-95cf-f7da108160ca",
                        "entry_id": "1ee75e82-1f64-3355-8862-518387408f7f",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "wetmatigheden"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d86b0ac7-5211-34ec-8f59-9349b0f590e3",
                        "entry_id": "1ee75e82-1f64-3355-8862-518387408f7f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "een samenhang die overal en altijd aanwezig is omdat ze gebaseerd is op natuurwetenschappelijke wetten"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "961070e5-620b-4602-947e-5d66ed390068",
                                "sense_id": "d86b0ac7-5211-34ec-8f59-9349b0f590e3",
                                "text": "Om maar relativerend te beginnen: die 7-procents-grens is zuiver arbitrair. Er is geen wiskundige wetmatigheid die van de grens van 7 procent een onhoudbare maakt."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "eaa495ac-c02e-38d7-a778-9d6cd9217663",
                        "entry_id": "1ee75e82-1f64-3355-8862-518387408f7f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "iets wat zo vaak voorkomt dat het een natuurwet lijkt te zijn"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0df2d9fd-7cc8-4e3a-ba4a-0eae6f6b3e00",
                                "sense_id": "eaa495ac-c02e-38d7-a778-9d6cd9217663",
                                "text": "In bepaalde kringen is het een jaarlijks terugkerend ritueel: zeuren over de presentatie van Zomergasten. Het interview gaat niet genoeg de diepte in, er is geen chemie, er wordt niet doorgevraagd, het is niet goed of het deugt niet. Janine Abbring wist aan deze wetmatigheid te ontkomen: een kniesoor daargelaten was iedereen onverdeeld positief over haar soepele presentatie."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f23bd040-a002-38a7-b782-485132c6d9e2",
                        "entry_id": "1ee75e82-1f64-3355-8862-518387408f7f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "iets wat in overeenstemming is met de (juridische) wet"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1f1b6543-0559-49e4-88fa-90838a6e3abe",
                                "sense_id": "f23bd040-a002-38a7-b782-485132c6d9e2",
                                "text": "Die structuur moet voor 1 januari een feit zijn en wordt momenteel binnen de gemeenten besproken. Vooral bij kleinere gemeenten ligt de positie van Enschede onder vuur. Zo wil Hellendoorn af van de wetmatigheid dat Enschede altijd voorzitter is van de Regio Twente en klonk in de gemeenteraad van Rijssen-Holten het geluid dat de Twentse agenda niet door Enschede bepaald mag worden."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5c227668-e3ba-4dc4-b91e-89e9c19542d1",
                        "source_entry_id": "1ee75e82-1f64-3355-8862-518387408f7f",
                        "source_sense_id": "d86b0ac7-5211-34ec-8f59-9349b0f590e3",
                        "target_lang_word": "natural law",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "natural law",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d6b644fc-84ee-338d-a0de-9147a09466fc",
                                        "entry_id": "7d1e6e7e-fc60-3326-8c0a-7923a3ffd459",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The set of universal legal or moral principles said to be discernible from nature by reason alone; one of these principles."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "93675377-6d30-4292-89af-df38f620726e",
                                                "sense_id": "d6b644fc-84ee-338d-a0de-9147a09466fc",
                                                "text": "Thus, for example, it is a natural law, that he who has been the author of any damage ought to repair it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "624de592-07d6-4f7a-bbc8-75b1428ab0bd",
                                                "sense_id": "d6b644fc-84ee-338d-a0de-9147a09466fc",
                                                "text": "For Maritain, natural law is not a written law; it is immanent in nature."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "872bd039-1da8-4d59-8931-68a97a5b8812",
                                                "sense_id": "d6b644fc-84ee-338d-a0de-9147a09466fc",
                                                "text": "The content of the natural law is the substantive account of ways of living that bring humanity to its natural good. In this broad sense, the natural law is much broader than law understood as a specific human institution."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c599c0c2-4b9d-34d5-959a-49c05ad02d25",
                                        "entry_id": "7d1e6e7e-fc60-3326-8c0a-7923a3ffd459",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A theory describing or positing such principles."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "97b5d101-18fc-483b-a83a-fbe0377e2ebc",
                                                "sense_id": "c599c0c2-4b9d-34d5-959a-49c05ad02d25",
                                                "text": "One of the reasons why it is sometimes felt that natural law is a predominantly rationalistic philosophy is because it has been associated with the concepts of the state of nature and of the original contract."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a442744-4072-401e-92e3-21123cc114be",
                                                "sense_id": "c599c0c2-4b9d-34d5-959a-49c05ad02d25",
                                                "text": "Another component of natural law is the view that some specific moral norms follow from these principles in such a way that it is easy for people to see their truth, even though it is possible, because of cultural distortion or personal immorality, that people be ignorant of them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "68488f20-1807-4f75-a82f-2e86414a1f6b",
                                                "sense_id": "c599c0c2-4b9d-34d5-959a-49c05ad02d25",
                                                "text": "Buckle […] argues that Grotius and Pufendorf understood Natural Law as a science of morals grounded in human nature."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4ff0568e-7221-3c4f-9bd2-50c2dc28380c",
                                        "entry_id": "7d1e6e7e-fc60-3326-8c0a-7923a3ffd459",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A law relating to natural phenomena, a law of nature."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "661ae780-e549-4fc9-9fa6-076f2fd937b4",
                                                "sense_id": "4ff0568e-7221-3c4f-9bd2-50c2dc28380c",
                                                "text": "It may seem an obvious objection that many of the Natural Laws have no connection whatever with the Spiritual World, and as a matter of fact are not continued through it. Gravitation for instance—what direct application has that in the Spiritual World?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "da5cef64-8727-402a-a50f-df13ab930ce2",
                        "source_entry_id": "1ee75e82-1f64-3355-8862-518387408f7f",
                        "source_sense_id": "d86b0ac7-5211-34ec-8f59-9349b0f590e3",
                        "target_lang_word": "rule",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "rule",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cd886ff0-71d9-3014-b445-df71cf2b773b",
                                        "entry_id": "e89300d6-99cd-34d3-a0e8-84a7c08e4c21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A regulation, law, guideline."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6749679-1039-4fb7-8ce9-594d8d11b0ea",
                                                "sense_id": "cd886ff0-71d9-3014-b445-df71cf2b773b",
                                                "text": "All participants must adhere to the rules."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d0015442-5938-4296-92ad-73c9835a8c25",
                                                "sense_id": "cd886ff0-71d9-3014-b445-df71cf2b773b",
                                                "text": "You have to follow the rules to enter the qualifiers for the football tournament."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ef86981d-e1ed-47a8-98c3-69dde3cc8f3e",
                                                "sense_id": "cd886ff0-71d9-3014-b445-df71cf2b773b",
                                                "text": "We profess to have embraced a religion which contains the most exact rules for the government of our lives."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a40dacf-e5a3-4bdc-9a53-4229e1997fbd",
                                                "sense_id": "cd886ff0-71d9-3014-b445-df71cf2b773b",
                                                "text": "The ability to shift profits to low-tax countries by locating intellectual property in them[…]is often assumed to be the preserve of high-tech companies.[…]current tax rules make it easy for all sorts of firms to generate[…]“stateless income”: profit subject to tax in a jurisdiction that is neither the location of the factors of production that generate the income nor where the parent firm is domiciled."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ea55d612-4425-3c02-99c0-5dafc2d40155",
                                        "entry_id": "e89300d6-99cd-34d3-a0e8-84a7c08e4c21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A regulating principle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bc806869-85e7-43ab-95cd-c75c35211ef6",
                                                "sense_id": "ea55d612-4425-3c02-99c0-5dafc2d40155",
                                                "text": "There's little can be said in 't; 'Tis against the rule of nature."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "19607e73-e1e9-3ab2-91f2-1786e6fee79a",
                                        "entry_id": "e89300d6-99cd-34d3-a0e8-84a7c08e4c21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of ruling; administration of law; government; empire; authority; control."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "517a77c2-a428-43f0-9340-4888cc2537d2",
                                                "sense_id": "19607e73-e1e9-3ab2-91f2-1786e6fee79a",
                                                "text": "Obey them that have the rule over you."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "62921139-7296-4509-b64a-8be5df39daca",
                                                "sense_id": "19607e73-e1e9-3ab2-91f2-1786e6fee79a",
                                                "text": "His stern rule the groaning land obeyed."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "60e66ef9-edc5-3e76-904e-ff977bf91d90",
                                        "entry_id": "e89300d6-99cd-34d3-a0e8-84a7c08e4c21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A normal condition or state of affairs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c410bbf4-7547-478f-810f-e188fb89cf18",
                                                "sense_id": "60e66ef9-edc5-3e76-904e-ff977bf91d90",
                                                "text": "My rule is to rise at six o'clock."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "35204486-2f0f-4b6c-8ea3-10cd1bba861b",
                                                "sense_id": "60e66ef9-edc5-3e76-904e-ff977bf91d90",
                                                "text": "As a rule, our senior editors are serious-minded."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "78820b97-2240-3d63-8d77-3e5f8b7285be",
                                        "entry_id": "e89300d6-99cd-34d3-a0e8-84a7c08e4c21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Conduct; behaviour."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1425e875-808d-49ea-ac40-65d782c10ce2",
                                                "sense_id": "78820b97-2240-3d63-8d77-3e5f8b7285be",
                                                "text": "This uncivil rule; she shall know of it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "63ad04a2-22ad-367c-8a8f-e99e6e1a0fae",
                                        "entry_id": "e89300d6-99cd-34d3-a0e8-84a7c08e4c21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An order regulating the practice of the courts, or an order made between parties to an action or a suit."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bec996c1-dccd-3468-8097-f04d41615c8d",
                                        "entry_id": "e89300d6-99cd-34d3-a0e8-84a7c08e4c21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A determinate method prescribed for performing any operation and producing a certain result."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a34a4386-4fbc-4ac0-a1f8-50a058e98932",
                                                "sense_id": "bec996c1-dccd-3468-8097-f04d41615c8d",
                                                "text": "a rule for extracting the cube root"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cad3d4a3-f7f8-31e7-b5f0-c9265dd7d3e4",
                                        "entry_id": "e89300d6-99cd-34d3-a0e8-84a7c08e4c21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A ruler; device for measuring, a straightedge, a measure."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "09680502-4b82-4a71-8656-d924e0dfabba",
                                                "sense_id": "cad3d4a3-f7f8-31e7-b5f0-c9265dd7d3e4",
                                                "text": "As we may observe in the Works of Art, a Judicious Artist will indeed use his Eye, but he will trust only to his Rule."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1f3f2d6e-6c3e-4f57-9897-66db0e4127d8",
                                                "sense_id": "cad3d4a3-f7f8-31e7-b5f0-c9265dd7d3e4",
                                                "text": "It is not right to pervert the judge by moving him to anger or envy or pity—one might as well warp a carpenter's rule before using it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0cdf03de-664f-3410-ab96-8bfef6a22188",
                                        "entry_id": "e89300d6-99cd-34d3-a0e8-84a7c08e4c21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A straight line (continuous mark, as made by a pen or the like), especially one lying across a paper as a guide for writing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e95b0fea-d125-3e26-ad9f-17c6e1545807",
                                        "entry_id": "e89300d6-99cd-34d3-a0e8-84a7c08e4c21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A thin plate of brass or other metal, of the same height as the type, and used for printing lines, as between columns on the same page, or in tabular work."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "dated",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "rule",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a5f8cb3f-22e6-3b26-ac32-ed661cff354a",
                                        "entry_id": "717d6401-c014-3011-88de-eb7a543e0e0d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To regulate, be in charge of, make decisions for, reign over."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "stative",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4175713-61db-4eeb-81b8-48ed0ef95b13",
                                                "sense_id": "a5f8cb3f-22e6-3b26-ac32-ed661cff354a",
                                                "text": "And Vickers launched forth into a tirade very different from his platform utterances. He spoke with extreme contempt of the dense stupidity exhibited on all occasions by the working classes. He said that if you wanted to do anything for them, you must rule them, not pamper them. Soft heartedness caused more harm than good."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7851f47d-fcc2-3193-8662-1f7597d4f071",
                                        "entry_id": "717d6401-c014-3011-88de-eb7a543e0e0d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To excel."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "slang",
                                            "stative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "52780f8a-e8fc-44cf-a7ea-5b5e8368b915",
                                                "sense_id": "7851f47d-fcc2-3193-8662-1f7597d4f071",
                                                "text": "This game rules!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a30c4493-88e6-31fd-93b1-53df61227976",
                                        "entry_id": "717d6401-c014-3011-88de-eb7a543e0e0d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To decide judicially."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ee0428ce-a1a4-4bda-96ed-d7ad9b3df63d",
                                                "sense_id": "a30c4493-88e6-31fd-93b1-53df61227976",
                                                "text": "The US supreme court has ruled unanimously that natural human genes cannot be patented, a decision that scientists and civil rights campaigners said removed a major barrier to patient care and medical innovation."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "22fb494e-3832-3c91-89ed-5102b0acbc35",
                                        "entry_id": "717d6401-c014-3011-88de-eb7a543e0e0d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To establish or settle by, or as by, a rule; to fix by universal or general consent, or by common practice."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8a873a56-bfba-4894-9eac-e2eebe5e452c",
                                                "sense_id": "22fb494e-3832-3c91-89ed-5102b0acbc35",
                                                "text": "That's a ruled case with the school-men."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "777d64af-cb9b-39f5-9d98-d1513e9aa401",
                                        "entry_id": "717d6401-c014-3011-88de-eb7a543e0e0d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To mark (paper or the like) with rules (lines)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
